{
  "name": "When to Call a Pro for Molding Repairs",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "It's easy to look at a dinged piece of molding and think, \"I can probably fix that myself,\" right? And sometimes you totally can! But there are definitely times when trying a DIY fix might actually make things worse or just not last. You should definitely consider calling in a pro like HH Remodeling LLC when the damage affects how your molding functions, or if it impacts the fit or timing of how pieces connect. If you've got issues with cooling lines or vents related to the molding, that's another big sign to bring in an expert. Anytime the repair needs complex disassembly, welding, precision refitting, or if you're worried about how the repair will look after it's done, it's smarter to get professional help. We're talking about situations where the molding might need to be fully taken apart and put back together just right, or if the overall quality of the molding is at stake. Don't risk a shoddy repair that you'll just have to fix again later. It's usually worth it to get it done right the first time, especially for tricky molding issues in your Denver area home. Give us a call at HH Remodeling LLC for a proper assessment; we're happy to help homeowners in places like Aurora, Centennial, and Cherry Hills Village.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
